Moti and I come home from the park.
Moti is very hungry.
I look at the clock.
It is exactly eight o'clock now.
Asha's rule is very clear.
Food must be given at exactly eight o'clock.
I take his metal bowl.
I put his food in the bowl.
Moti jumps up excitedly.
He wants to eat right away.
I say firmly, "Moti, wait!"
"Sit here!"
"You must not jump now."
Moti sits on the floor, but his tail wags quickly.
I place that bowl on the floor in front of him.
Moti looks at me.
I say, "This is your food."
"Eat it now."
Moti eats it happily.
